theory.intro:
A **power** is a short way of writing repeated multiplication. In $8^{3}$ the $8$ is the **base** and the $3$ is the **index**.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta}
\node[inner sep=0pt] at (0,0) {$a$};
\node[inner sep=0pt, font=\small] at (0.3,0.26) {$n$};
\node[font=\normalsize] at (0.8,1.3) {index};
\node[font=\normalsize] at (-0.4,-1.3) {base};
\draw[-{Stealth}] (0.66,1.05) -- (0.4,0.5);
\draw[-{Stealth}] (-0.34,-1.05) -- (-0.1,-0.3);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
